 "lesson": "Stellar structure and evolution",
 "title": "Massive stars live fast",
 "caption": "Fuel grows with mass but luminosity grows much faster (L ∝ M^3.5), so lifetime falls as t ∝ M/L ∝ M^(−2.5). With the Sun at 10 Gyr, a 2 M☉ star lasts about 1.8 Gyr; that is also the age of a cluster whose main-sequence turn-off is at 2 M☉.",
 "alt": "Main-sequence lifetime in billions of years against mass in solar masses, falling steeply from 10 at one solar mass to 1.8 at two.",
